      "text": "To determine how many minutes it will take for the printer to print 200 pages, we start by using the given rate of the printer, which is 17 pages per minute.\n\nWe can set up the problem using the formula:\n\\[\n\\text{Time (in minutes)} = \\frac{\\text{Total pages}}{\\text{Pages per minute}}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values into the formula, we get:\n\\[\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{200 \\text{ pages}}{17 \\text{ pages per minute}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we perform the division:\n\\[\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{200}{17}\n\\]\n\nCalculating the division:\n\\[\n\\text{Time} \\approx 11.7647\n\\]\n\nSince the problem asks for the answer to the nearest whole number, we round 11.7647 to the nearest whole number, which is 12.\n\nTherefore, the number of minutes it will take to print 200 pages is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{12}\n\\]",
