      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine how many minutes it will take for the printer to print 200 pages, we start by using the given rate of the printer. The printer prints 17 pages per minute.\n\nWe need to find the time \\( t \\) in minutes required to print 200 pages. We can set up the following equation based on the relationship between the number of pages printed and the time taken:\n\n\\[ \\text{Number of pages} = \\text{Rate} \\times \\text{Time} \\]\n\nSubstituting the known values into the equation, we get:\n\n\\[ 200 = 17 \\times t \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( t \\), we divide both sides of the equation by 17:\n\n\\[ t = \\frac{200}{17} \\]\n\nNow, we perform the division:\n\n\\[ t \\approx 11.7647 \\]\n\nSince we need to express the answer to the nearest whole number, we round 11.7647 to the nearest whole number, which is 12.\n\nTherefore, the time it takes to print 200 pages is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) minutes.",
